    "question": {
      ":question/id": "ce343e6c-bd09-50b5-a524-07352589f3cb",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following matrices are upper triangular matrices?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -11 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 11 & -9 \\\\ 8 & -10 & -11\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 0 & -9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}].$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The matrix $A$ is an upper triangular matrix since all the entries below the main diagonal are zeros.\n\nThe matrices $B$ and $C$ are *not* upper triangular matrices since they each have a non-zero element below the main diagonal: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{31} & =8\\ne 0 \\\\ {c}_{32} & =-4\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
